National Cleft Registry — Clone & Test Guide

1. Clone the repo
   git clone https://github.com/Gatoyah/national-cleft-register.git

2. Install dependencies (both apps)
   cd "Main Hub" && npm install
   cd "../Regional Hub" && npm install

3. Initialize databases
   Main Hub: npx drizzle-kit push
   Regional Hub: node init-db.mjs

4. Set environment variables (create .env files from .env.example or use absolute SQLite paths)

5. Set up default accounts
   Main Hub: curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/setup
   Regional Hub: curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/setup

6. Start servers
   Main Hub: npm run dev (port 3000)
   Regional Hub: npm run dev (port 3001)

7. Login
   Email: admin@ncr.gov.gh
   Password: Admin123!

8. Security features included
   - Passwords: bcrypt (12 rounds)
   - Sessions: SHA-256 hashed tokens
   - API keys: AES-256-GCM encrypted
   - Rate limits: login (5/15min), sync (10/min)
   - Audit logs: all actions logged
   - CSRF: HMAC-based token validation
   - Security headers: CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc.

Fixed bugs in this version:
- SQLite database paths (absolute paths in .env)
- Timestamp schema (integer with strftime('%s', 'now'))
- Sync validation (.nullable().optional() for null fields)
- Statistics SQL (integer timestamp comparison)
- Encryption key (fixed ENCRYPTION_KEY in .env)
